  "term": "neurosyphilis",
  "definition": "Neurosyphilis is an infection of the central nervous system caused by Treponema pallidum. It can be mild or unnoticed at first, may stay hidden for years, and can later appear in several forms, including stroke-like illness, progressive dementia, and other brain, spinal cord, or optic nerve problems.",
